CONSTRUCTORS-=====>

1->
Definition- Special member function. Name is same as class name. Called or invoked automatically when of object of its class is created. Always public. 

TYPES-=>

1->
Default constructor- Having no argument.
Syntax:
class classname
{
    public:
    classname()
    {
        code;
    }
};

2->
Parameterised constructor- Having argument.
Syntax:
class classname
{
    public:
    classname(argument)
    {
        code;
    }
};       

3->
Copy constructor- Class reference(&) passed as parameter in constructor.
Syntax:
constructor_name(classname &objectname);

OTHER-==>

1->
Constructor overloading- Multiple constructor with same name but different parameter.
Syntax:
class classname
{
    classname()
    {
        code;
    }
    classname(para1,para2.....)
    {
        code
    }
};

